We need answer. Need solve. Problem: satellite channel, sender transmits frames length 512B, data transmission rate sender 64 kb/s. Receiver returns very short acknowledgment frame. One-way propagation delay 270 ms. What is throughput for window sizes 1,7,17,117 respectively.

Need compute. Frame length 512 bytes = 512*8 = 4096 bits. Transmission rate 64 kb/s = 64,000 bits/s? Usually kb/s = 10^3? In networking, kbps = 1000 bps. Frame transmission time = 4096 / 64000 = 0.064 s = 64 ms. One-way propagation delay = 270 ms. RTT = 540 ms. Acknowledgment very short so transmission time negligible. Stop-and-wait (window=1): time per frame = transmission + RTT? Sender transmits frame, waits ack. Ack propagation back 270 ms. Total cycle = t_frame + 2*t_prop = 64 + 540 = 604 ms. Throughput = 4096 bits / 0.604 s = 6781.46 b/s = 6.78 kb/s ≈ 6.8 kb/s. So window=1 gives 6.8 kb/s. Choices: C has 6.8, 47.5, 64,64. Also maybe G 9.1 etc. So likely C.

Need verify for window sizes. With sliding window, throughput = min(data rate, window size * frame size / (t_frame + RTT?))? For window size W, if W frames can be in flight. Time to send W frames back-to-back = W * t_frame (if W*t_frame <= RTT? Actually cycle). Throughput = W * frame bits / (t_frame + RTT) if W frames sent per RTT+transmission? Need careful.

For window size W, sender can send up to W frames without waiting. If W is large enough to cover RTT, throughput limited by data rate 64 kb/s. For W=1: 6.8. For W=7: W * 4096 / (0.064 + 0.540) = 7*4096/0.604 = 28672/0.604 = 47470 b/s = 47.5 kb/s. For W=17: 17*4096/0.604 = 69632/0.604 = 115285 b/s > 64,000, so throughput = 64 kb/s (sender rate). For W=117: 64 kb/s. So C: 6.8, 47.5, 64,64. Yes.

